    45	## Limits
    46	- Busy workers and harness runs follow the run's limits (`auto.py status`; hard caps 5 workers (Ayush 27 Oct 22:20; auto.py:65), 2 harness). At most 2 new builds per run unless PLAN.md says otherwise.
    47	- Docker advice (27 Oct, after the 14:35 hang): spawn at most 2 Docker-heavy workers at once (QC, harden, build, kill test, blind scoring); check `auto.py status` and `docker ps` before each spawn. This is advice: auto.py does not count Docker-heavy workers (MAX_HARNESS caps paid runs, MAX_BUILDS caps new builds per run, nothing else).
    48	- Workers run anthropic/claude-opus-5-5, variant high. They cannot push, commit, use `gh`, queue the harness, or run auto.py. They may run `harbor run --agent oracle` and `--agent nop` (QC Step 10); every other `harbor run` stays denied. The permission applies to workers spawned after auto.py is restarted. The harness queue does not count these oracle/nop runs as paid-run slots.
    49	- Last spawn: no new spawn in the last 20 min before Until (PLAN.md `Last spawn:` may set another time) unless the step is named on PLAN.md's `Wind-down:` line (`auto.py spawn --wind-down`); auto.py refuses it otherwise.
    50	
    51	## Budget
    52	- Paid runs: at most 6 per day (IST), unless PLAN.md `Paid runs:` sets another number. auto.py counts the queue's runs started today plus queued ones and refuses `harness` at the cap.
    53	- A paid run starts only with no LIMIT and <= 2 busy workers; while a paid run runs, at most 3 busy workers (else 5). auto.py enforces both (`harness` refused, `spawn` held, MQ launch held through `auto_hold.json`).
    54	- The master counts as a worker when you count busy sessions for this rule.
    55	- Fresh usage window (after a reset or at the start of a run): start the paid run first, then fill the worker slots.
    56	- On LIMIT: hold spawns and paid runs, pause the queue, resume at the parsed reset + 5 min; the watcher writes a REPORT line and a macOS notification. Do not work around it.
    57	- Metered may run beside one other Docker-heavy job: Docker has 16 GiB now (B-N2 done 29 Oct).
    58	- Wind-down: after `AUTO STOP`, a paid run only via `harness --wind-down` for a task on PLAN.md's `Wind-down:` line, inside these caps. FINAL comes after the last worker result and the last harness run, or at the 2 h cap; at the cap busy workers are not aborted (the worker server stays up and REPORT.md says which pid to stop).
    59	- Stop now: `auto.py stop --now` stops the watcher and caffeinate and pauses the queue in one step; busy workers and RUNNING paid runs keep going and are listed under "Still running at stop".
    60	
    61	## Hard rules
    62	1. Never push, publish, submit, or commit. `pl_ready` is the end.
    63	2. Never edit templates, kit files, GOALS.md, LEVER_RULES, or this policy. Proposed changes go in REPORT.md.
    64	3. Never delete or overwrite a QC report, bundle, or harness job.
    65	4. Every decision goes to `decisions.jsonl` with `"by": "master (auto)"` and the policy row used: `python3 tools/decide.py --by "master (auto)" --slug <slug> --what "<decision; policy row>" [--words "<verbatim>"]`.
    66	5. After `AUTO STOP`: start nothing new (only `harness --wind-down` per the Budget section). On `FINAL`, finish REPORT.md and stop.
    67	6. Always give file links in REPORT.md for every prompt issued and every result read.
    68	
    69	## REPORT.md (`auto/runs/<run>/REPORT.md`, linked from `auto/LATEST`)
    70	Keep it current through the run: In short; Needs Ayush; Results per task; Decisions and overrides; Interrupted or unfinished (with times); Still running at stop (auto.py fills it at FINAL and on `stop --now`; "none" when nothing runs); Proposed changes. Times in IST (`TZ=Asia/Kolkata date`).

