/Users/mac/Desktop/Terminal Bench/Terminal_2.0_Harbor_Harness/Input_Bundle_QC/Final_checklist.md:335:Then build the execution copy. Step 10 never runs the bundle under review directly: it runs a tests-only copy that `exe_copy.py` builds from the exact bytes being shipped, and it never runs the judged channel at all.
/Users/mac/Desktop/Terminal Bench/Terminal_2.0_Harbor_Harness/Input_Bundle_QC/Final_checklist.md:337:Why tests-only. Harbor 0.24.0 runs the same verifier for every agent, and the oracle (uploads `solution/` and runs `solve.sh`), nop (does nothing) and stub agents make no model calls and leave no real trajectory. Run with the judge, the verifier either aborts (no `OPENAI_API_KEY`: rewardkit 0.2.1 raises "Missing credentials", writes no reward.json, and Harbor records a verifier error, not 0) or scores the trajectory criteria against an empty trajectory. Neither is evidence about the bundle. What Step 10 measures is whether the declared artifacts and the deterministic reward function agree, so it measures exactly that, with no key and no cost. The judged channel is still checked: gate 04 reads it, and `exe_copy.py` refuses to build unless `tests/judge.toml` loads under the rewardkit 0.2.1 schema. It is validated, never executed, and the sign-off says so.
