/Users/mac/Desktop/Terminal Bench/Terminal_2.0_Harbor_Harness/Input_Bundle_QC/Final_checklist.md:348:- rewrites `tests/reward.toml` to `weights = { test_output = 1 / positive total }` (full float), so every positive passing and no negative firing reads exactly 1.0 and doing nothing reads exactly 0.0 - the same channel the shipped bundle scores at half weight;
/Users/mac/Desktop/Terminal Bench/Terminal_2.0_Harbor_Harness/Input_Bundle_QC/Final_checklist.md:350:- drops the pre-baked OpenHands SDK install (S9 / DS-29) from `environment/Dockerfile`, which turns a multi-minute image build into seconds. It changes no score: the oracle uploads `solution/` and execs `solve.sh`, nop does nothing, and the stub is the oracle over a stub `solution/`, so none of the three ever starts an installed agent or reads `/opt/openhands-sdk-venv`. A real `openhands-sdk` run must use the bundle itself, never this copy;
