+
+### QC-failure table
+
+`python3 V3_fast_track_verify/scripts/count_qc_failures.py` scanned `QC/reports/*/v*.md`: **95 files, 17 task directories, 2,099 lines containing ❌, 85 distinct check IDs**. For each line with ❌, the script extracts all `AL|DS|TS|CL|JD|IN-N` IDs and counts each task directory once per ID. The v1 top table **matches exactly**: AL-27 13, DS-22 13, AL-2 12, TS-19 12, CL-2 12, AL-1 11, AL-18 11, CL-4 11, JD-18 11, CL-10 11, JD-7 10, DS-27 10, AL-4 10. This is a **report-mention** measure: ❌ in a checklist or comparison can count even if it references an earlier failure; it is not a count of independent defects.
+
+## 2. Timing and savings
+
+Command `python3 master_chat_work/20261030_upgrade2/S6_auto_speed/scripts/measure_lanes.py` read saved `/tmp/opencode-logs` only. Output: Nikhil three lanes 80/82/83 s job-sums and ALL_DONE 16:44:18, no solo same-byte baseline; warrant earlier gate 1,349/1,361/1,424 s oracle plus 240 s stub and 1,428 s owner, wall 14:18:51–15:40:53 = 82m02s (not purely serial); warrant later three lanes oracle 1,853/1,834/1,841 s plus 289 s nop, 265 s stub, 1,373 s owner, missing start timestamp in `runs.log`; cold-chain six sequential jobs 791/774/803/819/838/1,020 s, sum 84m05s and reported wall 84m37s (`QC/reports/cold-chain-backbone-quote/v5.md:91-94`). Different bytes and host load prevent causal lane savings; see S6 `FINDINGS.md:61-79`.
+
+| v1 number | Assessment | Basis / corrected wording |
+|---|---|
+| “15–45 min per gate” | **UNVERIFIED estimate** | No controlled same-tree 1-vs-3 lane gate. Warrant later wall roughly 66 min versus earlier 82 min is **INFERRED** from report time and missing log start, and has changed bytes/load (`S6_auto_speed/FINDINGS.md:74-79`). Cold-chain 35–45 min with three lanes is a model, not measured. |
+| “25–60 min per recheck” | **UNVERIFIED as a general saving** | `MEASURE.md:191-194` shows 18/24 rechecks repeat full gate; observed identical-tree outage repeat was ~10 min, warrant's *possible* future repeat 62–68 min was never run. A raw gate can cost 10–68 min; actual D4 eligible rechecks and kit-completion work were not measured. |
+| “12 h → 6–7 h” | **UNVERIFIED forecast** | The stated ≈5 h “two waits” is one outage timeline, not a cohort baseline; 31.3 h cold-chain wait is an outlier (`S6_auto_speed/FINDINGS.md:36-43`). Aggregate worker wait shares (85.7/245.1 h human/master; 55.5/245.1 h poll) include overlapping sessions and cannot be subtracted from task wall time (`MEASURE.md:72-108`). Measure same-stage pilot before promising a range. |
+
+## 3. Fit with Ayush's answers
+
+Section 4 of v1 is binding. Exact approval must use task, action, ceiling, frozen tree, expiry, evidence and plan-line ID. Missing percentage means the current **30%**, never a raised default (`FAST_TRACK_PLAN_v1.md:89-96`; `LEVER_RULES_v3.md` 1C). “No core → park” needs an exact plan line because `AUTO_POLICY.md:29` currently says never park. “Above gate → harden once” remains Needs Ayush. QC minor/warning may be noted for QL only under the exact approved condition, with the real QC verdict preserved. Manual paid-run authority starts only **after QC PASS and freeze**, within the day's cap, with Ayush told and the decision logged; `AUTO_POLICY.md:26,51-53` already pins the auto-side conditions. v2 adds an explicit manual preflight. Full QC always runs its full Step 10; reuse is recheck-only (`P11_full_qc_v3.md:29-35`). No paid result is ever reused (`AUTO_POLICY.md:28-29`).
+
+**Open interpretation:** the live QC kit says five oracle runs in Step 10 (`Input_Bundle_QC/Final_checklist.md:354-367,390`), while P12 normally saves three and proposed D4 spot checks one (`P12_recheck_fix_v4.md:67`; v1 step 10). Existing P11 explicitly labels x3 as Ayush's exception and “not kit-complete” until x5 (`P11_full_qc_v3.md:89-90`). The v2 plan keeps the reuse option but requires a kit-complete gate before a paid run unless Ayush explicitly approves cross-session aggregation; `QUESTIONS.md` asks that narrow question.
+
