+## 2. Timing and savings
+
+Command `python3 master_chat_work/20261030_upgrade2/S6_auto_speed/scripts/measure_lanes.py` read saved `/tmp/opencode-logs` only. Output: Nikhil three lanes 80/82/83 s job-sums and ALL_DONE 16:44:18, no solo same-byte baseline; warrant earlier gate 1,349/1,361/1,424 s oracle plus 240 s stub and 1,428 s owner, wall 14:18:51–15:40:53 = 82m02s (not purely serial); warrant later three lanes oracle 1,853/1,834/1,841 s plus 289 s nop, 265 s stub, 1,373 s owner, missing start timestamp in `runs.log`; cold-chain six sequential jobs 791/774/803/819/838/1,020 s, sum 84m05s and reported wall 84m37s (`QC/reports/cold-chain-backbone-quote/v5.md:91-94`). Different bytes and host load prevent causal lane savings; see S6 `FINDINGS.md:61-79`.
+
+| v1 number | Assessment | Basis / corrected wording |
+|---|---|
+| “15–45 min per gate” | **UNVERIFIED estimate** | No controlled same-tree 1-vs-3 lane gate. Warrant later wall roughly 66 min versus earlier 82 min is **INFERRED** from report time and missing log start, and has changed bytes/load (`S6_auto_speed/FINDINGS.md:74-79`). Cold-chain 35–45 min with three lanes is a model, not measured. |
+| “25–60 min per recheck” | **UNVERIFIED as a general saving** | `MEASURE.md:191-194` shows 18/24 rechecks repeat full gate; observed identical-tree outage repeat was ~10 min, warrant's *possible* future repeat 62–68 min was never run. A raw gate can cost 10–68 min; actual D4 eligible rechecks and kit-completion work were not measured. |
+| “12 h → 6–7 h” | **UNVERIFIED forecast** | The stated ≈5 h “two waits” is one outage timeline, not a cohort baseline; 31.3 h cold-chain wait is an outlier (`S6_auto_speed/FINDINGS.md:36-43`). Aggregate worker wait shares (85.7/245.1 h human/master; 55.5/245.1 h poll) include overlapping sessions and cannot be subtracted from task wall time (`MEASURE.md:72-108`). Measure same-stage pilot before promising a range. |
+
+## 3. Fit with Ayush's answers
+
+Section 4 of v1 is binding. Exact approval must use task, action, ceiling, frozen tree, expiry, evidence and plan-line ID. Missing percentage means the current **30%**, never a raised default (`FAST_TRACK_PLAN_v1.md:89-96`; `LEVER_RULES_v3.md` 1C). “No core → park” needs an exact plan line because `AUTO_POLICY.md:29` currently says never park. “Above gate → harden once” remains Needs Ayush. QC minor/warning may be noted for QL only under the exact approved condition, with the real QC verdict preserved. Manual paid-run authority starts only **after QC PASS and freeze**, within the day's cap, with Ayush told and the decision logged; `AUTO_POLICY.md:26,51-53` already pins the auto-side conditions. v2 adds an explicit manual preflight. Full QC always runs its full Step 10; reuse is recheck-only (`P11_full_qc_v3.md:29-35`). No paid result is ever reused (`AUTO_POLICY.md:28-29`).
+
+**Open interpretation:** the live QC kit says five oracle runs in Step 10 (`Input_Bundle_QC/Final_checklist.md:354-367,390`), while P12 normally saves three and proposed D4 spot checks one (`P12_recheck_fix_v4.md:67`; v1 step 10). Existing P11 explicitly labels x3 as Ayush's exception and “not kit-complete” until x5 (`P11_full_qc_v3.md:89-90`). The v2 plan keeps the reuse option but requires a kit-complete gate before a paid run unless Ayush explicitly approves cross-session aggregation; `QUESTIONS.md` asks that narrow question.
+
+## 4. Breakage and test baseline
+
+| Boundary | What a change could break | Existing pin and required regression check |
+|---|---|---|
+| LIMIT, paid concurrency | A new manual path or dockslot could bypass hold or launch at >2 busy; four worker sessions could run beside paid work. | `auto.py:86-92,1238-1254,1554-1590`; `auto/tests/test_auto.py:668,744,782,803,1158,1213`. Test LIMIT and max busy before/after paid start. |
+| FIFO, flock, resume | A priority/backfill scheduler could reorder spend or lose an auto-resume after usage limit. | `master_queue.py:147-164,612-628,643-665`; `scripts/tests/test_master_queue.py:126,136,338`. Keep FIFO; test shared lease integration under the existing lock. |
+| Tree refusal | Reuse/manifests or manual harness could bypass freeze. | `tools/intake.py:46-74,150-157`; `tools/repackage_one.py:78-84`; `tools/tests/test_upgrade_tools.py:158,164,208`. Recompute tree sha immediately before reuse and before queue add. |
+| Worker permission | Moving to `~/tb_runs` will fail for spawned workers unless external-directory allowlist changes; broadening it may expose other home files. | `auto.py:114-144`; `auto/tests/test_auto.py:395,1260`. Allow only the exact runs root, preserve deny on paid Harbor, auto and queue. |
+| Docker cleanup | A new tag or lease must not kill someone else's same-task container; existing prefix cleanup is broad. | `master_queue.py:272-308`; `scripts/tests/test_master_queue.py:163,295`. Keep existing cleanup until owner-scoped test passes; never prune images or pass Harbor `--delete` (`P11_full_qc_v3.md:76`). |
+| Prompt/QC rules | F2/F3/D4 can weaken live kit or omit a required run. | `P11_full_qc_v3.md:37,74-105`; kit `Final_checklist.md:335-367,390-391`; P12 `:59-75`. Snapshot templates and kit hash, verify checklist coverage. |
+
+**Runs performed under OUT temp only:** `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 TMPDIR=OUT/tmp python3 -m unittest discover ...`.
+
+| Suite | Baseline result | Constraint / evidence |
+|---|---|---|
+| `auto/tests` | 73 run; 49 pass, **24 errors**, 0 assertion failures | Every error is loopback `ThreadingHTTPServer(("127.0.0.1",0))` bind denied by this sandbox (`auto/tests/test_auto.py:604`; `OUT/auto_test.log` summary). **UNVERIFIED** under normal host permissions. |
+| `tools/tests` | 30 run; 27 pass, **3 failures**, 0 errors | Ran a mirror inside OUT because tests hard-code `/tmp` (`test_upgrade_tools.py:35`, `test_e3_e6_tools.py:38`) and repackage writes `/tmp` (`repackage_one.py:86`). Only path literals in mirror changed; `OUT/scripts/prepare_tools_test_mirror.py`. Failures are stale live fixture expectations: cold-chain expected tree `8ca9c267f59b`, current `c10ae543512d`; district expected “not met”, current output “MET” (`OUT/tools_test.log`). The original suites were not edited. |
+| `scripts/tests` | `unittest discover`: 0 collected (exit 5); **not a green suite** | Harness tests are pytest-style (`scripts/tests/test_master_queue.py:126`, `test_run_wrapper.py:20`). Default Python also lacks pytest/httpx; harness `.venv/bin/python` imported them but unittest collected 0 (`OUT/harness_test.log`). A pytest baseline is still needed in the authorized build environment; some tests spawn fake processes, so not run under this session's no-kill rule. |
+
+## 5. Design holes
+
+| Area | Finding, evidence | v2 fix / verification |
+|---|---|---|
+| D2 lock/lease | MQ already uses `flock` around state (`master_queue.py:147-164`); dockslot must use a separate lock and never acquire locks in opposite order. A PID-only lease risks PID reuse; a dead wrapper may leave its Docker child alive. `docker events --help` confirms command/filter syntax, **not daemon event delivery**; `docker info --format '{{.NCPU}} {{.MemTotal}}'` returned `0 0` then socket permission denied here. | Lease ID + PID/PGID/start time, heartbeat, run ID/container identity, TTL; reconcile Docker state before freeing uncertain lease; fail closed. Events as wake-up only with timed fallback. Fake dead/wrong-PID/daemon-restart tests; live event check later when Docker accessible. |
+| D2 memory charge | `MEASURE.md:30-35` has a single verifier snapshot, not task peaks. `master_queue.py:546-551` reads task.toml or 4096 MB default. Thus a never-measured task has no “peak.” | Persist per-job measured peak from sampled `docker stats` with task/phase/tree and sample window; charge peak ×1.5 when present, else task.toml memory, as Ayush answered. Unknown/incomplete samples fall back to task.toml. Verify charge provenance in status. |
+| D4 evidence | P12 result has scalar rewards and tree sha but no per-trial paths, exit status, run identity or stub (`P12_recheck_fix_v4.md:67,73`); warrant raw jobs in `/tmp` (`RECHECK_FIX.md:108-122`). | Manifest: exact tree hash, kit/tool versions, copy recipe/diffs, every run's result/reward/reward-details/log path, successful exit, no exception, expected values, ALL_DONE, immutable hashes. Require three oracle, nop, owner, stub and any kit additions or fall back. Spot oracle+nop on same tree; compare rewards and report that reuse is an exception. |
+| D6 parsing/refusal | `plan_fields()` first matching line wins (`auto.py:484-500`); duplicate or prose line can silently win. `tools/decide.py:35-65` records `by/slug/what/words`. | Canonical pre-approved line ID/hash; reject duplicate/malformed/expired/cross-task/changed-tree/unknown percentage/missing measurement/over cap; write exact line and measured evidence with `decide.py --what` and REPORT. New notify command must popup **and sound**, and master calls it on every manual or auto Needs-Ayush stop. |
+| A5 lint | Bad prompt: cold-chain go fixes judge and demands predicted ≤35 (`.../20261030T1200_go_cap60.md:5-9`); schema QC note says each oracle once (`.../schema-migration-plan-repair/20261030T0245_qc.md:103`) contrary to its own x3 count at `:89-90`; Nikhil fix says shipped data byte-identical unless directions say otherwise (`.../b7c42.../20261030T1745_fix.md:29`) and directions require changed fixtures (`:35-45`). Decisions record cold-chain correction (`decisions.jsonl:544-545`). | Syntax lint can catch unresolved tokens, illegal count phrasing, gate/exception mismatch and contradiction candidates. Reachability needs numeric calculation/attestation by master. `--force-lint` must log a reason; no general `--no-lint` in production. Last ten files by mtime had zero unresolved `[[...]]`/`<SHA>` and zero “oracle x1/once” literal from the command in this session; **UNVERIFIED that all ten are good**. Path checks must distinguish future OUT/job paths, `/app` container paths and absent existing inputs, else false positives. Replay bads and all ten. |
+| F2/F3 vs kit | Kit is authority (`P11_full_qc_v3.md:37`; kit `Starter.md` and `Final_checklist.md`). P12 currently allows skip Docker when only docs changed (`P12_recheck_fix_v4.md:67`), while a P11 recheck still runs all gates (`P11_full_qc_v3.md:32`). P2 kill table already tests generic solvers (`P2_build_v5.md:66`); do not imply it lacks all. | Receipt supplements G1–G7, does not replace them; F3 adds two specific solvers and P9 design blind only when new core/lever; P11 full remains full; recheck reuse gets explicit non-kit-complete label until x5 decision. Verify kit diff and template coverage. |
+| Pre-QC Codex | S7 `FINDINGS.md:10-18,47-49` proposes read-only Codex but says exact output confinement untested. This V3 sandbox could read a sample bundle and write OUT: `test -r .../bundles/cold-chain-backbone-quote/task.toml` → 0, `test -w` on that file → 1, `test -w VERIFY_REPORT.md` → 0. This does not prove `codex exec -s read-only -o OUT` works or prevents all bundle writes. | Pilot with a disposable copied bundle and host hash before/after. Invoke Codex with input read-only and OUT-only output under a tested host sandbox; treat failures as reports, not automatic fixes. No Codex paid run was authorized here. |
+| D5 `/tmp` coverage | Active writers/instructions: `_COMMON_RULES_v5.md:17`; P11 `:42,49,76,79-85,99`; P9 `:70`; P12 `:67`; P13 blind `:7,21`; P16 `:13`; P17 `:19,31`; `auto.py:137-140` permission; `master_queue.py:54`; `repackage_one.py:86`. Old template versions and `P6_oracle_nop_stub_v2.md:12` also mention `/tmp`; MQ `HOME=/tmp` is **inside a container**, not a host artifact (`master_queue.py:62`). Docker settings file `~/Library/Group Containers/group.com.docker/settings-store.json` exists but top-level 16 keys contain no sharing directory list (read-only JSON key scan); `~/tb_runs` mount permission is **UNVERIFIED**. | Inventory active issued/templates and code, change only host durable paths, keep historical files as snapshots. Prove Docker bind mount works before switching. Update WORKER_PERMISSION narrow allowlist. |
+
+## 6. Order, dependencies and missing gates
+
+D1 must precede D6 because `Paid runs:` is parsed loosely (`auto.py:498-500`). D5 must precede D4 because raw jobs now disappear under `/tmp` (`RECHECK_FIX.md:108-122`). Dockslot must precede a production lane increase; the same-tree 1/3/4 benchmark needs empty Docker (`MEASURE.md:208-210`). **Correction:** D2 integration should remain FIFO and keep MQ flock and external Harbor accounting; priority/backfill would be a separate behavior change, not part of this fast track. D5 must include worker permissions and Docker file sharing before any worker switches. D6's manual paid-run preflight must precede its new permission.
+
+Missing gates: migrate old free-form `Paid runs:` plans; add tests for exact/no-cap/duplicate line, D6 scopes, notify sound, dockslot dead lease and double-counting, D4 incomplete/mismatched results, and path permissions; run harness pytest in its virtual environment when permitted; snapshot old policy/templates, update `prompts/templates/CHANGELOG.md` and rule fingerprints/hash manifests; document rollback per component, without reverting active work. Switch on between runs, after smoke under real loopback/Docker permissions. The v1 “all three suites green” cannot be claimed from this sandbox (section 4).
+
+### Every wrong or missing item and fix
+
+| Item | Required fix in v2 |
+|---|---|
+| D6 popup/authority | Include master-hold caller, add sound and audited manual paid-run preflight. |
+| D2 process visibility | Preserve current external Harbor detection; cover arbitrary worker Docker. |
+| F2 existing safeguards | Extend P12 G1–G7 rather than replacing or describing them as absent. |
+| D4 raw evidence/stub | Persist manifest and stub; refuse incomplete reuse. |
+| D5 permissions/sharing | Narrow WORKER_PERMISSION allowlist and mount proof before move. |
+| A5 impossible static guarantee | Numeric attestation and warning tier; avoid false path refusals. |
+| Kit x5 vs reuse | Label exception and settle paid-run readiness (question 1). |
+| Timing/12h promise | State hypotheses, measure matched pilots. |
+| Test gate | Fix stale fixtures, run pytest suite, get real loopback/Docker smoke before release. |
