+### QC-failure table
+
+`python3 V3_fast_track_verify/scripts/count_qc_failures.py` scanned `QC/reports/*/v*.md`: **95 files, 17 task directories, 2,104 lines containing ❌, 85 distinct check IDs** on the final scan. An earlier scan in this live directory saw 2,099 such lines; other sessions were active, so the corpus was not frozen. The task counts below stayed the same. For each line with ❌, the script extracts all `AL|DS|TS|CL|JD|IN-N` IDs and counts each task directory once per ID. The v1 top table **matches exactly**: AL-27 13, DS-22 13, AL-2 12, TS-19 12, CL-2 12, AL-1 11, AL-18 11, CL-4 11, JD-18 11, CL-10 11, JD-7 10, DS-27 10, AL-4 10. This is a **report-mention** measure: ❌ in a checklist or comparison can count even if it references an earlier failure; it is not a count of independent defects.
